.TH OWNER-AUDIT 1 "2026-10-13" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
owner-audit \- find numeric file owners not resolved by the host name service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B owner-audit
.RB [ --scope " user|group|both" ]
.RB [ --one-file-system ]
.RB [ --null ]
.I DIRECTORY
.br
.B owner-audit
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Checks UID/GID lookups through the operating system's configured name
service using getpwuid and getgrgid. Does not modify ownership. Failed
lookups can result from temporary NIS/LDAP failures as well as deleted accounts.
Symbolic links are examined with lstat but not followed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --scope user|group|both
Select which identity classes to check (default: both).
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Do not descend into other devices.
.TP
.B --null
Emit NUL-terminated ISSUE, UID, GID, PATH fields without summary.
.TP
.BR --help , --version
Display help or version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 scan completed; 1 incomplete scan; 2 usage error; 3 required library missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR getent (1)
